# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Outwait — ONE .gitignore for the whole repo.
#
# This is a single git repo, rooted here. Inside it there are three separate
# npm projects (backend/, frontend/, component/) with no workspace linking
# them, but they ship together and they travel together.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# API keys, deploy keys, and the Convex deployment name all live in .env.local.
# Nothing here ever goes public.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
secrets.json


# ── Dependencies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/releases


# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
dist-ssr/
build/
out/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo


# ── Convex local state ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .convex/ is the local backend binary + its data. .convex-tmp/ is the codegen
# scratch dir we point CONVEX_TMPDIR at so it stays on the same drive.
.convex/
.convex-tmp/


# ── Notes and planning ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The whole strategy lives in markdown: MASTER-PLAN, DESIGN, PROGRESS, the
# competition sweep, the phase-by-phase thinking. That stays on this machine.
*.md

# RANKING.md is the competitive sweep — every other submission, scored. Useful
# to us, not something to hand the people we are being scored against.
RANKING.md

# ...except the two files the judges are meant to read.
# hackathon.md at the repo root is a HARD hackathon requirement — leaving it
# out is a disqualification, so this line is not optional.
!hackathon.md
!/README.md
!/LICENSE.md


# ── Agent and editor tooling ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local dev tooling, not part of the product.
.claude/
.agents/
.cursor/
.vscode/
.idea/
.playwright-mcp/
*.code-workspace


# ── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*


# ── Test and coverage ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
.nyc_output/


# ── Caches ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.eslintcache
.cache/
.temp/
.tmp/
temp/
tmp/


# ── OS and editor noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.local

# Local MCP config — machine-specific absolute paths, not useful to anyone else
.mcp.json


# ── Video and social scratch at the repo root ────────────────────────────────
# Frames, crops and exports made while cutting the demo video land here as
# throwaways. Anchored with a leading slash on purpose: this ignores loose
# images at the REPO ROOT only, and never touches frontend/public/brand/ or
# docs/screens/, which are real assets the README and the app both point at.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.gif
/*.mp4
/*.mov
/*.webm
